#   pl.system.sync_all(core_type=pl.SyncCoreType.MIX)
#   run_second_message_wave_with_the_same_tokens()
#
# REPEATED-TASK CLOSURE (optional, required when one physical core runs more
# than one logical mailbox task in the same epoch):
#
#   AIC task end:
#       wait(MAILBOX_FREE_EVENT)       # drain the final mailbox ack
#       wait(STORE_FREE_EVENT)         # drain the final MTE3/store ack
#       pl.system.bar_all()            # local PIPE_ALL after final event op
#
#   AIV task end:
#       set(STORE_FREE_EVENT, MTE3)     # final store lifetime is complete
#       pl.system.bar_all()            # local PIPE_ALL after final event op
#
# After the drains, outstanding event credit is zero.  A later task may omit
# its first FREE wait only because the previous task and both local barriers
# proved the physical resources reusable; it is NOT consuming a saved/FIFO
# event token.  The remaining messages wait on acknowledgements generated by
# their own task.  Do not put either bar_all under `sub_rows > 0`.
#
# This closure does not allow tokens to cross sync_all(MIX), and `bar_all()` is
# not a replacement for MIX.  A real gate must exercise per-core depths just
# below and at the observed failure threshold, the production uneven owner
# distribution, and the maximum dynamic task count.  MlaProlog needed depths
# 3, 4, uneven 4/5, and dynamic 36/37 (1024 tasks over 28 cores).

